  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "Passive: battle-start summon guards; Active: heal guards, refill guard, then guards absorb ally damage",
    "skill1": "healing over time on guards and two weakest allies",
    "skill2": "summon ranged marksman; armor-piercing shots increase ranged damage taken and amplify allied summon ranged damage",
    "skill3": "haste bonus rises when two guards remain on field",
    "skill4": "during ultimate, guards alternate AoE slashes that grant shield; aura boosts nearby melee damage, extra for summons",
    "skill5": "when enough allied summons from different allies are alive, buff all summons ATK and Phys and Magic DEF"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Peggy]] opens with **two royal guards** and reaches her ultimate quickly thanks to high starting energy. Her ultimate **heals guards to full** then routes most ally damage through them while **reducing HP-loss damage** they take, giving broad protection once it lands. Royal Scroll provides **strong healing over time** on guards and the weakest allies, while Royal Barrage adds a marksman that **amplifies ranged damage** on front targets and boosts summon output. Ex aura and Supreme buffs also make her a **summon-team amplifier** beside her protector role. Protection **depends on the ultimate window** and living guards — burst that kills her or denies the cast leaves allies exposed.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Peggy]] opens with **two royal guards** and a **fast first ultimate** that heals them and routes ally damage through the summons while she heals and amps ranged and summon lines. Once the absorb window lands, hero focus fire wastes itself on guards. Cancel that opening ultimate with [[Lily May]], or **delete [[Peggy]]** before guards stabilize with [[filter:assassin-delete]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Himmel]]. Spread pressure across **guards and [[Peggy]]** so the protection package never locks."
}